	"department": "PSYCH",
	"description": [
		"This course offers students the opportunity to explore the developmental stage of emerging adulthood (ages 18-25) during one month of study/travel in China. Students employ a psychological perspective to read and discuss literature about the influence of culture, gender, history, and current issues on development during this critical milestone in the lifespan. Interactions and field projects with the group's hosts at universities and research sites in China provide firsthand experience and foster cross-cultural comparisons. Counts toward psychology, Asian studies, Chinese, and women's and gender studies majors; and Asian studies and women's and gender studies concentrations. Offered alternate years during Interim. Prerequisite: PSYCH 125 or a course in Asian studies or women's and gender studies, or permission of instructor; PSYCH 241 or PSYCH 249 strongly recommended."
	],
